{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "engine": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 2
  },
  "slug": "pyauto-api-first-page-only",
  "title": "342 open tickets, and the report says 30",
  "screen": {
    "type": "data",
    "level": 1,
    "data": {
      "workspace": "sla_report.py, the weekly overdue-ticket report, Kestrel Facilities (fictional)",
      "flags": [
        {
          "id": "ask",
          "label": "Service manager, Leah Moss",
          "text": "Your report says 30 tickets are open, every week. The helpdesk screen says 342. Which is it? The client review is at 16:00.",
          "when": "true",
          "severity": "info"
        },
        {
          "id": "seen",
          "label": "Pattern",
          "text": "The count is always exactly 30.",
          "when": "not isNull(lookAt) and not fixed",
          "severity": "warning"
        },
        {
          "id": "lock",
          "label": "Client review",
          "text": "16:00: the client review used the wrong count.",
          "when": "not isNull(lockedAt)",
          "severity": "error"
        }
      ],
      "charts": [],
      "tables": [],
      "code": [
        {
          "id": "code",
          "label": "sla_report.py",
          "language": "Python",
          "lines": [
            {
              "id": "c0",
              "text": "r = session.get(BASE + '/tickets', params=dict(status='open'), timeout=10)",
              "when": "fix == \"bug\"",
              "mark": "not isNull(lookAt) ? \"error\" : \"none\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "text": "tickets = r.json()",
              "when": "fix == \"bug\"",
              "mark": "not isNull(lookAt) ? \"error\" : \"none\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "text": "url = BASE + '/tickets?status=open&per_page=100'",
              "when": "fix == \"follow\"",
              "mark": "\"changed\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c3",
              "text": "while url:",
              "when": "fix == \"follow\"",
              "mark": "\"changed\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c4",
              "text": "    r = session.get(url, timeout=10); r.raise_for_status()",
              "when": "fix == \"follow\"",
              "mark": "\"changed\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c5",
              "text": "    tickets += r.json(); url = r.links.get('next', dict()).get('url')",
              "when": "fix == \"follow\"",
              "mark": "\"changed\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c6",
              "text": "r = session.get(BASE + '/tickets', params=dict(status='open', per_page=1000), timeout=10)",
              "when": "fix == \"big\"",
              "mark": "\"warning\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c7",
              "text": "tickets = r.json()",
              "when": "fix == \"big\"",
              "mark": "\"warning\""
            },
            {
              "id": "c8",
              "text": "for p in range(1, 13): tickets += session.get(BASE + f'/tickets?status=open&page=' + str(p)).json()",
              "when": "fix == \"guess\"",
              "mark": "\"warning\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "meters": [
        {
          "id": "due",
          "label": "Client review",
          "value": "16:00"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "objective": "Handle error status codes, rate limits and pagination",
  "secondaryObjectives": [
    "Call an HTTP API with urllib.request or Requests, setting headers, query parameters and a timeout"
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "cite": "GitHub Docs, Using pagination in the REST API",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-17",
      "url": "https://docs.github.com/en/rest/using-the-rest-api/using-pagination-in-the-rest-api",
      "note": "Read 2026-11-17 through a summarizing fetch. Large responses are paginated (an issues list 'will only return 30 issues'); 'the response headers will include a link header'; 'The URL for the next page is followed by rel=\"next\"'; the guide's script keeps requesting while a next link exists. The case's ticket API is fictional and follows the same convention."
    },
    {
      "cite": "Author's scenario (REQ-333)",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-17",
      "note": "Every organization, person, count and deadline is invented teaching data; tool output is an authored rendering in the tool style."
    }
  ],
  "brief": {
    "situation": "You maintain sla_report.py at Kestrel Facilities (fictional). It pulls open tickets from the helpdesk API and lists those past their SLA. It has reported exactly 30 open tickets for weeks; the helpdesk screen shows 342. The client review is at 16:00. It is 15:05.",
    "handover": [
      "The helpdesk API documents paginated lists with a Link header, rel=\"next\".",
      "The API allows at most 100 items per page."
    ],
    "howItWorks": [
      "Pick a step from the action list: look, change, check or ship. Nothing you pick is typed or executed: every step shows an authored result.",
      "Each step takes working minutes, and the clock moves by the minutes it takes. The deadline runs on the same clock.",
      "Shipping is final for this case. Afterwards you record what you found and explain your reasoning."
    ]
  },
  "clock": {
    "start": "15:05",
    "tick": "1min",
    "maxDuration": "150min",
    "calendar": "clock"
  },
  "params": {
